# ==============================================================================
# CYBERTRADE TERMINAL // BACKEND CONFIGURATION (.env)
# ==============================================================================
# CyberTrade Terminal is built with a resilient Local-First architecture.
# It works immediately out of the box using encrypted, multi-user isolated
# local storage with one-click JSON/CSV backup & restore capabilities.
#
# To enable Cloud Multi-Device Sync, provide either Supabase OR Firebase credentials below:

# OPTION 1: SUPABASE INTEGRATION (Recommended for PostgreSQL + Row-Level Security)
# 1. Create a project at https://supabase.com
# 2. In Project Settings > API, copy your Project URL and Anon Public Key:
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...

# OPTION 2: FIREBASE INTEGRATION (Authentication + Cloud Firestore)
# 1. Create a project at https://console.firebase.google.com
# 2. Add a Web App and copy the config parameters:
VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=AIzaSy...
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=cybertrade-journal.firebaseapp.com
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=cybertrade-journal
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=cybertrade-journal.appspot.com
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=123456789012
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=1:123456789012:web:abcdef123456

# GENERAL CONFIGURATION
VITE_APP_NAME="CyberTrade Terminal"
VITE_DEFAULT_CURRENCY="$"
